Package: scRefAudit
Type: Package
Title: Reference Composition Sensitivity Analysis for Single-Cell Annotation
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(person("Xiaowei", "Chu", email = "xiaoweichu873@gmail.com",
    role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0007-4333-8334")),
    person("Caixia", "Lyu", role = "ctb"))
Description: Fits balanced entropic optimal transport on a fixed cost matrix,
    reuses curvature across reference-composition scenarios, generates
    derivative-guided perturbations, and ranks cells for annotation review.
    The R interface uses the bundled Python numerical implementation through
    'reticulate'. Both matched-total-variation and log-weight perturbations
    are supported. Sensitivity describes dependence on reference weights.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: reticulate (>= 1.41), stats, utils
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.10), NumPy (>= 1.26), SciPy (>= 1.11)
NeedsCompilation: no
